            <ArticleTitle>Piriformis pyomyositis, an unusual presentation of leg pain post partum--case report and review of literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1505-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3109/14767058.2011.636098</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Piriformis pyomyositis is defined as a subacute infection of skeletal muscles associated with systemic infectious symptoms. In the literature it rarely occurs postpartum. We report a case of piriformis pyomyositis involving a parturient and review the published cases available in the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
